  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>

<para>For 1 - 4 use the problem below:</para>


<blockquote>
  Priya is buying raisins and almonds to make trail mix. Almonds cost $5.20 per pound and raisins cost $2.75 per
  pound. Priya spent $11.70 buying almonds and raisins. The relationship between pounds of almonds, pounds of
    raisins, and the total cost is represented by the equation \(5.2a+2.75r=11.7\).
</blockquote>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="141ee309-47d6-4ef8-a902-faf57beecc60"><problem><para>
      <para>How many pounds of raisins did Priya buy if she bought the following amount of almonds:</para>
      <para>2 pounds of almonds</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>1.192</para><para>2.75</para><para>0.946</para><para>0.473</para></problem><solution><para>0.473</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 0.473. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
